    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="b9f9517d-b708-518e-b03e-ec8253656487" activityNameId="3064e658-05e1-5d73-a251-8a19550c8419" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Electronic passive elements, washing machine, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Electronic passive elements, washing machine, at plant
The material requirements are based on the measured average weight of the different parts (diodes, capacitors, etc.) and of an average composition of the parts. Transport distances are standard distances for the raw materials.;
UUID: 9c0e2df6-7ee2-3b42-979d-55913ecb6ee9
This process describes the material and related transport requirements for the electronic parts (without printed wiring boards) of a washing machine.
Location: The electronic passive elements are for a Swiss washing machine for a household.
Technology: Electronic passive elements for an actual washing machine for a household.
Time period: The material composition of the electronic parts is based on data from 2001. Weight and number of the elements of the PWBs were collected 2004.
Production volume: na
Sampling: unknown 
Extrapolations: Material composition of the electronic parts are extrapolated from the mobile communication technology.
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_9c0e2df6-7ee2-3b42-979d-55913ecb6ee9.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
